// PARAM: --analysis parity
// The acceptance case for Parity as a public analysis: a property provable
// from parity information alone. n is completely unconstrained, so no
// interval or sign reasoning bounds x or y at all -- but times_parity has
// PEven * _ = PEven, so 2*n is Even whatever n is, and 2*n+1 is then Odd.
// Even and Odd are disjoint, so x and y can never be equal; parity refutes
// the equality and therefore proves its negation.
// Multiplication by the literal 2 is what makes this non-relational: the
// domain evaluates each operand independently, so n+n would be Top+Top=Top
// (it cannot see the two operands are the same value), while 2*n is Even
// from the literal's own parity alone.
// This exercises the full public path: AnalysisConfig resolves
// --analysis parity to Plan_Parity Solver_Join, Analyse_Dispatch routes it
// to analyse_parity_report, and that report reads the routed-unit solved
// AnalysisResult through lookup_context -- the same generic pipeline the
// other three domains use, with no Parity-specific result or report
// construction anywhere in it.
void main() {
  n := __voblint_nondet_int();
  x := 2 * n;
  y := 2 * n + 1;
  __voblint_check(!(x == y)) // PROVED
}
